1
00:00:10,007 --> 00:00:16,418
HireStream is the official overseas placement portal of HPSEDC, the Government of Himachal Pradesh.

2
00:00:16,478 --> 00:00:19,947
Registration is free, and HPSEDC never asks for money.

3
00:00:20,007 --> 00:00:22,431
The portal works in English and Hindi.

4
00:00:22,491 --> 00:00:25,372
Use the language button at the top to switch.

5
00:00:25,432 --> 00:00:27,333
To begin, open Create Account.

6
00:00:27,393 --> 00:00:35,896
Enter your full name, your email address and a password of at least eight characters, with a capital letter, a number and a symbol.

7
00:00:35,956 --> 00:00:40,145
Type the password again to confirm it, then click Create Account.

8
00:00:40,205 --> 00:00:42,237
You are signed in straight away.

9
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:54,851
The application form has four pages, and the bar at the top shows how far you have got.

10
00:00:54,911 --> 00:00:59,285
Before you start, keep your passport and Aadhaar card in front of you.

11
00:00:59,345 --> 00:01:01,376
There is nothing to upload today.

12
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:09,485
Page one asks for your identity documents: passport number, expiry and issue dates, place of issue, and your ECR or ECNR status.

13
00:01:09,545 --> 00:01:14,109
If you do not have a passport yet, tick the box, and you can still apply.

14
00:01:14,169 --> 00:01:16,833
Your Aadhaar number is checked as you type.

15
00:01:16,893 --> 00:01:26,019
Then fill in your personal details exactly as printed on your passport, your mobile and WhatsApp numbers, your email, and your permanent address.

16
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:29,060
Your answers are saved each time you click Next.

17
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:06,505
On page two, pick the work you can actually do.

18
00:03:06,565 --> 00:03:08,766
You can choose up to three trades.

19
00:03:08,826 --> 00:03:16,346
Some trades, such as driver, nurse, caregiver, electrician and welder, ask a few extra questions on the next page.

20
00:03:16,406 --> 00:03:21,599
Then choose the languages you speak, and how well you speak and write each one.

21
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:25,390
If your language is not listed, type it in and click Add.

22
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:34,573
Page three asks for your highest qualification.

23
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:37,149
For school classes you choose your board.

24
00:03:37,209 --> 00:03:42,364
For ITI, diploma or a degree, you choose your university or college, or type it in.

25
00:03:42,424 --> 00:03:44,815
Next come the questions for your trade.

26
00:03:44,875 --> 00:03:50,784
A driver gives their licence number, class and expiry date, and says whether they hold a badge.

27
00:03:50,844 --> 00:03:59,518
Use the plus and minus buttons to set your months of experience, pick the specific skills you have, and add your last employer if you wish.

28
00:03:59,578 --> 00:04:03,539
You only prove these details with documents if you are selected.

29
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:12,087
Page four shows your whole application, section by section.

30
00:05:12,147 --> 00:05:13,988
Use Edit to correct anything.

31
00:05:14,048 --> 00:05:19,495
Print or Save PDF gives you a printed copy of the application form for your records.

32
00:05:19,555 --> 00:05:22,970
When everything is correct, click Submit application.

33
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:26,510
You can come back and update your details at any time.

34
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:38,800
After submitting, your dashboard opens.

35
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:44,632
You will see your registration number, which you should quote when you call HPSEDC.

36
00:05:44,692 --> 00:05:48,918
To apply for jobs, you must first confirm your email address.

37
00:05:48,978 --> 00:05:52,010
HPSEDC sends a six digit code to your email.

38
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:54,610
Type it in the box and click Confirm.

39
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:59,810
If the code has not arrived, check your spam folder or ask for a new code.

40
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:08,344
Open Find a Job to see the vacancies HPSEDC has open.

41
00:06:08,404 --> 00:06:13,866
Search by job title or skill, or filter by country, category, experience and salary.

42
00:06:13,926 --> 00:06:17,022
Each job shows how well it matches your profile.

43
00:06:17,082 --> 00:06:24,714
Click a job to read the details: the employer, the country, the salary, and the documents you would need if selected.

44
00:06:24,774 --> 00:06:25,765
Click Apply Now.

45
00:06:25,825 --> 00:06:35,430
Your application then appears under My Application, where you can follow its progress through four stages: applied, interview, selected and placed.

46
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:44,343
HPSEDC interviews every applicant.

47
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:54,639
When your interview is scheduled, you are notified, and it appears in My Application with the date, time and place, or a meeting link for a video interview.

48
00:06:54,699 --> 00:06:58,202
Click Confirm attendance so HPSEDC know you will come.

49
00:06:58,262 --> 00:07:03,878
If the time does not suit you, use Reschedule to explain why and suggest another time.

50
00:07:03,938 --> 00:07:06,782
If you can no longer attend, choose Decline.

51
00:07:06,842 --> 00:07:09,950
You can also add the interview to your calendar.

52
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:46,391
If you are selected, your dashboard lists the documents HPSEDC now need: a police clearance certificate, a medical fitness certificate, your passport, identity proof, education and experience certificates, and any document your trade or the destination country requires.

53
00:07:46,451 --> 00:07:49,045
Click Complete your travel documents.

54
00:07:49,105 --> 00:07:53,422
Upload a photo or scan of each one in PDF, JPG or PNG format.

55
00:07:53,482 --> 00:07:55,072
HPSEDC then check them.

56
00:07:55,132 --> 00:08:06,121
On the last page, Before you travel, tell HPSEDC how far you have got with your police clearance, medical test and insurance, then click Save my progress.

57
00:08:06,181 --> 00:08:09,350
Replies from HPSEDC appear on your Help page.

58
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:12,751
When HPSEDC upload your signed appointment letter, your offer is ready.

59
00:09:12,811 --> 00:09:14,554
Open it from My Application.

60
00:09:14,614 --> 00:09:20,735
It shows the salary, the start date and the country, and you can view or print the offer letter.

61
00:09:20,795 --> 00:09:21,894
Read it carefully.

62
00:09:21,954 --> 00:09:25,757
Click Accept Offer to confirm, or Decline and give a reason.

63
00:09:25,817 --> 00:09:28,847
Offers have a deadline, so do not wait too long.

64
00:09:28,907 --> 00:09:35,929
Once you accept, you are placed, and your dashboard tracks the remaining pre-departure steps until you travel.

65
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:25,793
Help is always one click away.

66
00:10:25,853 --> 00:10:29,841
Ask HPSEDC opens a message thread with the placement team.

67
00:10:29,901 --> 00:10:32,074
They reply during working hours.

68
00:10:32,134 --> 00:10:34,796
For a formal complaint, use Grievances.

69
00:10:34,856 --> 00:10:45,752
Choose a category, such as someone asking you for money, a problem at your workplace abroad, or a problem with your application, then describe what happened.

70
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:48,893
The bell at the top shows your notifications.

71
00:10:48,953 --> 00:10:53,778
Remember: HPSEDC never asks for money to register or to get you a job.

72
00:10:53,838 --> 00:10:56,430
If anyone does, report it immediately.

